      "description": "Half the trunk rather than a quarter of it: either both front quadrants, both back, both upper or both lower, so one of the two cutting planes disappears and the two quadrants read as a single field with no seam where they meet. Between a third and three-fifths of the horse. Which plane survives and which side of it is pale are both settled at birth.",
